| `poly` | Started studies in polytechnics |
| `tyke_3kk` | Unemployment period of more than three months |
| `syntyv` | Birth cohort |
| `female` | Female |
| `vuosi_yoL` | Year of upper-secondary/matriculation qualification |
| `nuts2` | Region of birth at NUTS2 level |
| `use_EducationPGS_5` | EA-PGS quintile used in interaction figures |
| `use_PC1`-`use_PC10` | Genetic principal components |
| `use_sample` | Source health survey |
| `sfm_PRS` | Indicates whether the parental EA-PGS comes from the mother or father |

Parental education and income are taken from the non-genotyped parent, while the EA-PGS is taken from the genotyped parent. `sfm_PRS` is included as a control for whether the EA-PGS comes from the mother or father. Parental income is based on average taxable income in 2001-2009.

The GxE model uses manually created product terms. `pedu_PRS` is the product of parental education and parental EA-PGS. `faminc1_PRS`, `faminc2_PRS`, and `faminc3_PRS` are generated for the three parental-income categories. The middle-income category is the reference group, so only `faminc1_PRS` and `faminc3_PRS` enter the interaction model.

The continuous `use_Educational_attainment_PRS` is used in the models reported in Table 2, while `use_EducationPGS_5` is used for Figures 2 and 3.


## Timing of annual covariates

Child born, employment, unemployment, and psychotropic medication use are measured in the same year as the event `stop_applying`. Starting studies in polytechnics is defined using entry in autumn of year *t-1* or spring of year *t*, following the coding used in the previous study on re-application behavior.
